iption><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bengal-tamil-nadu-assam-and-puducherry-brace-for-closely-watched-bypoll-verdicts/articleshow/134793524.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bengal-tamil-nadu-assam-and-puducherry-brace-for-closely-watched-bypoll-verdicts/articleshow/134793524.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T21:21:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794790,imgsize-231846.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India to come out with a national plan to boost small-scale fisheries sector]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-to-come-out-with-a-national-plan-to-boost-small-scale-fisheries-sector/articleshow/134794725.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794725.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-to-come-out-with-a-national-plan-to-boost-small-scale-fisheries-sector/articleshow/134794725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-to-come-out-with-a-national-plan-to-boost-small-scale-fisheries-sector/articleshow/134794725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T21:20:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishwa Mohan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794788,imgsize-87558.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Govt proposes prior approval for ads of Schedule H, H1 and X drugs]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-proposes-prior-approval-for-ads-of-schedule-h-h1-and-x-drugs/articleshow/134794693.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794693.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-proposes-prior-approval-for-ads-of-schedule-h-h1-and-x-drugs/articleshow/134794693.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-proposes-prior-approval-for-ads-of-schedule-h-h1-and-x-drugs/articleshow/134794693.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T21:16:04+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794816,imgsize-95370.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Welcome to India': Rahul Gandhi reacts to Musk's remarks; Starlink boss says 'thank you']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/welcome-to-india-elon-rahul-gandhi-responds-to-musks-starlink-remarks/articleshow/134794474.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794474.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi has weighed in on Elon Musk's comments about the hold-up of Starlink's commercial operations in India. Musk voiced his exasperation over regulatory obstacles, suggesting that oligarchs sway the industry. The government swiftly countered, emphasising the fairness of its regulations among satellite operators and underlining the importance of security compliance for safeguarding users and data alike.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/welcome-to-india-elon-rahul-gandhi-responds-to-musks-starlink-remarks/articleshow/134794474.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/welcome-to-india-elon-rahul-gandhi-responds-to-musks-starlink-remarks/articleshow/134794474.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T21:01:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794511,imgsize-31048.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[INDIA bloc protests against CEC: 'Unite to fight' proposes Uddhav's Sena; will AAP, DMK relent?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-block-protests-against-cec-unite-to-fight-proposes-uddhavs-sena-will-aap-dmk-relent/articleshow/134793601.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134793601.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Uddhav Thackeray's Shiv Sena has called on AAP and DMK to join opposition forces against CEC Gyanesh Kumar over irregularities in SIR. Despite AAP's separation from the INDIA bloc and DMK's mixed reactions, the lack of participation from both factions underscores existing rifts in the opposition landscape. Analysts argue that these parties might still rally together to uphold democratic principles, though future collaboration remains clouded by their historical rivalries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-block-protests-against-cec-unite-to-fight-proposes-uddhavs-sena-will-aap-dmk-relent/articleshow/134793601.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-block-protests-against-cec-unite-to-fight-proposes-uddhavs-sena-will-aap-dmk-relent/articleshow/134793601.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T20:55:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kunal Varma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134795119,imgsize-1326886.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Musk goes on rant after India rejects ‘oligarch’ claim: What makes Starlink controversial]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/musk-goes-on-rant-after-india-rejects-oligarch-claim-what-makes-starlink-controversial/articleshow/134794140.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794140.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/musk-goes-on-rant-after-india-rejects-oligarch-claim-what-makes-starlink-controversial/articleshow/134794140.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/musk-goes-on-rant-after-india-rejects-oligarch-claim-what-makes-starlink-controversial/articleshow/134794140.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T20:43:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794271,imgsize-114044.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Remain alert, stay indoors': India issues advisory for citizens in Saudi Arabia amid Houthi attacks]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-alert-stay-indoors-india-issues-advisory-to-citizens-in-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-attacks/articleshow/134794137.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794137.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-alert-stay-indoors-india-issues-advisory-to-citizens-in-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-attacks/articleshow/134794137.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-alert-stay-indoors-india-issues-advisory-to-citizens-in-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-attacks/articleshow/134794137.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T20:41:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794265,imgsize-112304.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['BJP's poll campaign has begun': Mann on CBI raids on OSD, 5 others]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-poll-campaign-has-begun-mann-on-cbi-raids-on-osd-5-others/articleshow/134793940.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134793940.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Punjab's Chief Minister Bhagwant Mann has leveled allegations against the BJP, claiming the use of Central investigative agencies for political leverage. He interpreted the recent CBI raids on his office as a signal of an impending election campaign. Mann reiterated his dedication to the interests of Punjab's citizens, dismissing corruption claims and drawing parallels with similar tactics in other states with non-BJP leadership.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-poll-campaign-has-begun-mann-on-cbi-raids-on-osd-5-others/articleshow/134793940.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-poll-campaign-has-begun-mann-on-cbi-raids-on-osd-5-others/articleshow/134793940.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T20:30:19+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794012,imgsize-81823.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bajrang Dal says no volunteers to be mobilised at Jantar Mantar on October 10]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bajrang-dal-says-no-volunteers-to-be-mobilised-at-jantar-mantar-on-october-10/articleshow/134792218.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134792218.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Bajrang Dal firmly refuted claims of organizing a gathering at Jantar Mantar on October 10 for their demonstration. The group expressed discontent over being linked to potential violence against protesters. CJP co-convener Ashutosh Ranka voiced concerns over right-wing groups being mobilized for violent purposes. Bajrang Dal confidently stated that the protest would not succeed due to insufficient public backing, reinforcing their long-standing disapproval of disruptive protests across the nation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bajrang-dal-says-no-volunteers-to-be-mobilised-at-jantar-mantar-on-october-10/articleshow/134792218.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bajrang-dal-says-no-volunteers-to-be-mobilised-at-jantar-mantar-on-october-10/articleshow/134792218.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T19:15:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134792465,imgsize-144204.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India’s data silos cost up to 7% of welfare spending, threaten AI push: Report]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-data-silos-cost-up-to-7-of-welfare-spending-threaten-ai-push-report/articleshow/134791638.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791638.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India processes over 20 billion UPI transactions monthly and has enrolled more than 1.4 billion Aadhaar users. However, fragmented government databases are causing financial losses and excluding eligible beneficiaries from welfare schemes. Past data-cleaning efforts have shown significant savings, but data systems largely operate independently, limiting their effectiveness. The report emphasizes the importance of accurate and accessible data for improving governance and deploying AI.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-data-silos-cost-up-to-7-of-welfare-spending-threaten-ai-push-report/articleshow/134791638.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-data-silos-cost-up-to-7-of-welfare-spending-threaten-ai-push-report/articleshow/134791638.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:47:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791945,imgsize-131054.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Dhappa' gets a Day 3 twist as police allow Rahul, INDIA bloc MPs to protest at Raj Ghat]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dhappa-gets-a-day-3-twist-as-police-allow-rahul-india-bloc-mps-to-protest-at-raj-ghat/articleshow/134791827.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791827.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Opposition leaders, after previously being stopped by police, successfully reached Raj Ghat for their protest. They staged a brief sit-in to honor Mahatma Gandhi while voicing their concerns about electoral integrity. Congress leaders accused the government and Election Commission of undermining democratic rights and engaging in a conspiracy. Rahul Gandhi emphasized the need for justice regarding these electoral issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dhappa-gets-a-day-3-twist-as-police-allow-rahul-india-bloc-mps-to-protest-at-raj-ghat/articleshow/134791827.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dhappa-gets-a-day-3-twist-as-police-allow-rahul-india-bloc-mps-to-protest-at-raj-ghat/articleshow/134791827.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:47:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791905,imgsize-194934.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Air India Delhi-Riyadh flight returns after Houthi attack on Saudi airport; flights ops suspended till October 10]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-delhi-riyadh-flight-returns-after-houthi-attack-on-saudi-airport/articleshow/134791563.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791563.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-delhi-riyadh-flight-returns-after-houthi-attack-on-saudi-airport/articleshow/134791563.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-delhi-riyadh-flight-returns-after-houthi-attack-on-saudi-airport/articleshow/134791563.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:42:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791727,imgsize-43116.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre to unveil AI regulation roadmap within a month; industry to shoulder safety responsibility]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-to-unveil-ai-regulation-roadmap-within-a-month-industry-to-shoulder-safety-responsibility/articleshow/134791615.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791615.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a major initiative, the Centre will unveil a consultation paper in the coming month to propose new regulations for artificial intelligence. These guidelines are set to focus on safety, inclusivity, and the handling of emerging threats such as deepfakes and psychological effects. The responsibility for implementation will lie primarily with industry leaders within a techno-legal framework, accompanied by a roadmap for developing homegrown GPUs.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-to-unveil-ai-regulation-roadmap-within-a-month-industry-to-shoulder-safety-responsibility/articleshow/134791615.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-to-unveil-ai-regulation-roadmap-within-a-month-industry-to-shoulder-safety-responsibility/articleshow/134791615.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:42:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791818,imgsize-68783.cms"/></item></channel></rss>